Theorem 13 survives the audit as stated, with a corrected description of what the proof uses. Statement: for k = 9 there is no real Williams family of pairwise distinct nonconstant members of degree <= 3, with any leading signs. This is conditional on Theorem 10, Lemmas 3, 6 and 24, and the sign-free extension, all previously PROVED.

Proof outline:
1. Reduction to 9 cubics, or 8 cubics + 2t+1, in the normal form f_i = 2t+1 + t(t+1)(a_i t + c_i), with a_i > 0 and u_i^2 < 8v_i, (1-u_i)^2 < 8v_i.
2. An exact a priori bound. Since V = H, the identity H - 2^-8 t^8 = 2^-8 sum_{j>=1} t^(8-2j)(t+1)^(2j) e_2j(h/g) >= 0 holds. Together with the even boundary equations this gives Re(-7/5) - lam Phi = q2 S^2 + q1 S + qB M20 + q0, exactly:
   - 9 cubics: lam = 59/110, (q2, q1, qB, q0) = (-2/55, -788/125, -2/55, 39391023/1100000);
   - 8 + lin: lam = 27/50, (q2, q1, qB, q0) = (-1/25, -678/125, -1/25, 1294023/50000).
   With Phi < 729/32 (resp. 585/32) and M20 >= 0, this gives S < 7.31054 (resp. S < 6.29891).
3. Exact Farkas certificates, 57 and 52, covering S in [9/32, 3849/512] and [1/4, 203/32]. They use only:
   - the measure relaxation with mass m and sum v = S on the closed capped domain;
   - the two reflection-even boundary equations;
   - P <= S*M12/2;
   - Phi_V >= 0, the order-2 consequence of Phi = 2^-10 (e2(beta) + e2(gamma));
   - Ve(t0) >= 2^-8 t0^8 for t0 in {-19/5, 0, 1/5, 3/5, 4/5}.
   No N3 tangent cut and no third-order identity is used.

Once the notebook's ingredient list is corrected, degree <= 3 stays open only for odd k >= 11.

Candidate Theorem 13 is not refuted. Components (i) and (iii) and check (a) reproduce independently. Statement: no real Williams family of degree <= 3 exists for k = 9, in either case (9,0) or (8,1). This rests on the reduction to those cases with a_i > 0, which this audit did not re-audit.

The proof needs only the following:
- the two reflection-even boundary equations E0 = Ve(-1) - 2^-8 = 0 and E1 = Ve'(-1) + 2^-5 = 0;
- Cauchy-Schwarz, 0 <= M11^2 <= S M12;
- Phi = Ve''(-1) - 56/256 >= 0, i.e. Taylor order 2;
- global positivity Ve(t0) >= 2^-8 t0^8 at t0 in {-19/5, 0, 1/5, 3/5, 4/5}, and at t0 = -7/5 for the S-bound;
- Phi < 729/32 (9 cubics) or 585/32 (8 + lin).

These give S < 7.31054 (9 cubics) and S < 6.29891 (8 + lin). The 57 + 52 exact Farkas certificates then cover S in (9/32, 7.517578] and (1/4, 6.34375], and those ranges contain the remainder.

The N3L/N3U cuts and the third-order identity are not used. The notebook's account of which cuts each S-range uses should be corrected as listed under gaps.
